	<description>One snowy night a famous Hollywood actor slumps over and dies onstage during a production of King Lear. Hours later, the world as we know it begins to dissolve. &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Moving back and forth in time—from the actor's early days as a film star to fifteen years in the future, when a theater troupe known as The Travelling Symphony roams the wasteland of what remains—this suspenseful, elegiac, spellbinding novel charts the strange twists of fate that connect five people: the actor, the man who tried to save him, the actor's first wife, his oldest friend, and a young actress with the Traveling Symphony, caught in the crosshairs of a dangerous self-proclaimed prophet. &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Sometimes terrifying, sometimes tender, &lt;i&gt;Station Eleven&lt;/i&gt; tells a story about the relationships that sustain us, the ephemeral nature of fame, and the beauty of the world as we know it."</description>
